/* The truncation of the Stumpff series in spacelab-astro `kepler::stumpff`, certified (plans/17
   Ф28.B).

   Inside |w| <= 1/32 the code takes
     C(w) ~ 1/2 - w/24 + w^2/720 - w^3/40320 + w^4/3628800,
     S(w) ~ d6 - w/120 + w^2/5040 - w^3/362880 + w^4/39916800,
   d6 the double `1.0 / 6.0` folds to; every other coefficient is exact (the divisions by 24, 120,
   ... run at run time, and their rounding is evaluation error, not this file's). Each sign of w is
   its own function of s = sqrt|w| in [0, sqrt(1/32)]: C = (1 - cos s)/s^2 and S = (s - sin s)/s^3
   for w = s^2, (cosh s - 1)/s^2 and (sinh s - s)/s^3 for w = -s^2. supnorm_lib.sollya's `split`
   encloses sup |p/f - 1| on each. S's bound is about three times its first dropped term, because
   d6 alone is 2^-54 = 5.55e-17 off at w = 0.

   The CANDIDATE lines are not a gate (plans/17 Ф28.B part 2): fpminimax's degree-4 polynomial in w
   with double coefficients, against the Taylor polynomial to w^20 (whose own truncation is below
   1e-80 relative here), and supnorm's bound on it. C's is 16 times closer than the shipped series;
   S's cannot beat the 2^-54 its constant term costs.

   cd derivations && timeout 300 sollya kepler_stumpff_supnorm.sollya                            */

execute("supnorm_lib.sollya");

d6 = round(1/6, D, RN);
b = round(sqrt(1/32), prec, RU);

split("kepler_stumpff_C_pos", x^2 * (1/2 - x^2/24 + x^4/720 - x^6/40320 + x^8/3628800), 1 - cos(x), b, 48);
split("kepler_stumpff_C_neg", x^2 * (1/2 + x^2/24 + x^4/720 + x^6/40320 + x^8/3628800), cosh(x) - 1, b, 48);
split("kepler_stumpff_S_pos", x^3 * (d6 - x^2/120 + x^4/5040 - x^6/362880 + x^8/39916800), x - sin(x), b, 48);
split("kepler_stumpff_S_neg", x^3 * (d6 + x^2/120 + x^4/5040 + x^6/362880 + x^8/39916800), sinh(x) - x, b, 48);

h = 1/32;
tc = 0; ts = 0;
for k from 0 to 20 do { tc = tc + (-x)^k / fact(2*k + 2); ts = ts + (-x)^k / fact(2*k + 3); };
mc = supnorm(fpminimax(tc, 4, [|D, D, D, D, D|], [-h; h], relative), tc, [-h; h], relative, acc);
ms = supnorm(fpminimax(ts, 4, [|D, D, D, D, D|], [-h; h], relative), ts, [-h; h], relative, acc);
print("CANDIDATE kepler_stumpff_C fpminimax degree 4:", dec4(sup(mc), floor(log10(sup(mc))) - 3, true));
print("CANDIDATE kepler_stumpff_S fpminimax degree 4:", dec4(sup(ms), floor(log10(sup(ms))) - 3, true));
quit;
